nters":[{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:9731\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1946-06-01/pdf/FR-1946-06-01.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: 5bf55716d98db6c95e0939c795f0b1662681c3240784be53875ba8252f72b6bf\nLocation: 11 FR 5893, PDF pages 1-3 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 1 of 92 ===\n^ x o n a l ^\nFEDERAEGISTE\nVOLUME 1 1 '•'%. '9 3 4  -tf»* < /a/ited % NUMBER 107\nWashington, Saturday , June 1, 1946\nThe President\nPROCLAMATION 2692 \nF lag D ay, 1946\nBY TH E PR ESID EN T O F TH E U N ITED  ST A T E S \nO F A M E R IC A \nA  P R O C L A M A T IO N\nWHEREAS on June 14,1777, the Con­\ntinental Congress adopted the flag \nwhich we cherish as the flag of the \nUnited States of America; and\nWHEREAS under this flag generations \nof Americans have lived and worked to \nestablish the foundations of our country’ s \ngreatness; and\nWHEREAS this flag has become the \nbeloved symbol of our way of life, our \nachievements as a people, and the many \nblessings which Providence has heaped \nupon us; and\nWHEREAS for many years it has been \ncustomary to observe the anniversary of \nthe day of the adoption of the flag as \nFlag Day; and\nWHEREAS in this year following our \ngreat victories on the field of battle it is \nespecially appropriate that we continue \nthe customary observance of this day, . ,  \nand ","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_9731.txt","sha256":"8772e8178b53a589537c4016350dab8a58934d0cd8ea7b142f164572929a7f27","source":{"line":396,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"6d15bab3f50cac6e88ea8cc82439b67a5201643b26148591de6e63f776dd8ae8"}}]}
